      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "4cd942e356469c40841235bbaee6301ca21e52bca5c7e958ef8958bfb0a9f9f5",
      "new_sha256": "86e711e2ba50e26619ed8fb03c6757316cbb1d4a534c5491eb6290484b6d4f4f",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5577",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Recall that the matrix $P_S = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T$ maps any vector $\\mathbf x\\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nIn our case, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/assets/fde70db50cff408347bdebc086fbfa3ae87020bb0300b32dad67168d617ed607.png) Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot (14)^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/example-5577.json",
          "file_sha256": "208be2987e0a0158124355f215f0a8ab56859f7d608947f5f41cd305382956a0"
        }
