        {
          "question": "e-8316",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ onto the plane whose parametric equation is $\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{v} + t\\mathbf{w}$, where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/assets/bd8680b251ca871c0912f7aa85826bc705f022d12155fa1ddc73e2d01c30d2ca.png)",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/example-8316.json",
          "file_sha256": "f1e59d41273683a411efb646ddc760e9fe1d852555c479bda48307e8642fd7dd"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2591,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 2592
    },
    {
      "question": "e-8316",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "3116267e7358b491bb21351c2a12c255230620392338353b55659949ceff240a",
      "new_sha256": "ababa35fbed664c449696c53484ed39114ce3a6b012ad1ce3df717e0b996c088",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8316",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Recall that the matrix $P_S = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T$ maps any vector $\\mathbf x\\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nNotice that the plane $\\mathbf{r}=s\\mathbf{v}+t\\mathbf{w}$ is actually the subspace $\\text{Span}\\{\\mathbf{v}, \\mathbf{w}\\}.$ \nHence, we have \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/assets/af442d03acdc13db51c3ae53fcf250074e9adc2d4ed4bd2f52e6e76b5d4c2fe8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/example-8316.json",
          "file_sha256": "f1e59d41273683a411efb646ddc760e9fe1d852555c479bda48307e8642fd7dd"
        }
      ],
