    {
      "question": "e-5578",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "9a9eb54182b9eb52d0731b0e8fb52db726cfd0b4ebc43442b58dbb0dc5f9e533",
      "new_sha256": "8359c990d27f994c09ffda434b16c0991ce3a6c0b36e83be9fe982cbb3cdd2af",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5578",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if $Q^2=Q$ and $Q^T=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n$A^T = A$\nbut \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{T}\\ne B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is an orthogonal projection matrix. Indeed,\n$C^T = C$\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\"",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/example-5578.json",
          "file_sha256": "3f9fee1120e35566339431db8b8db56053498bcb389fdf590c779e37e6b333b2"
        }
      ],
