    {
      "question": "e-5580",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "32183681f26c3519e0132eb529197e9339595a379a71d5fdfe441f84180f40ee",
      "new_sha256": "b73cd02c8dc1d5836c577819f86cae88f4150a85901ad2c7a72cff4a3a3d4882",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5580",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we find the orthogonal projection matrix onto $S^\\perp = \\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}\\}.$\n\nUsing the formula for the orthogonal projection matrix\n\n$$\nP_{S^\\perp} = \\mathbf{a} (\\mathbf{a}^T\\!\\mathbf{a})^{-1} \\mathbf{a}^T,\n$$\n\nwe obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{{S}^{\u22a5}} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={6}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $P_S  + P_{S^\\perp} = I.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =I-{P}_{{S}^{\u22a5}} \\\\  & =I-\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p_{13} + p_{32} = (-2) + (-2) = -4.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071876/example-5580.json",
          "file_sha256": "287ee1850d22d8c3346ab5598c9e0450a488274b6388477179df3f0f7342919e"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 2591,
